#: processes/sdlc/code-quality-gates.bpmn:136
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Bean `16ei`, arc `3fva`. After Task_RepositoryGates, WHATEVER it concluded (`needs: gates` with `always()`), `qa:publish --github` writes this run's `test/results` trees to the orphan `qa-reports` branch: `main/<sha>/` on a push to main, `pr/<n>/<head-sha>/` on a same-repository PR (owner rulings D1, D3). A fork PR's token is read-only, so it is skipped with a `::notice` naming why. It does NOT reach GW_Join: a red publish is its own red and never decides mergeability, and the hard gates never wait on it. The only job here holding `contents: write`, which is also how `bun run gates` knows not to run it locally. A CALL ACTIVITY: the key derivation, the fork skip and the never-`-f` retry loop are `qa-publish.bpmn`, which also draws the retention run that takes entries off the branch again."
