#: processes/sdlc/code-quality-gates.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "FOUR QUESTIONS, ONE RUNNER — bean `7fu5`. They were four jobs (`lean-bare-import`, `python-imports`, `rust-wildcard`, `dependency-advisories`), each about a second of work behind a ~13 s checkout and a runner request; measured on `main` run 37133247484 (2026-10-03), the run took 21.7 min while its longest job executed for 174 s, the rest waiting for runners. Now they are steps of the `hygiene` job, and every step after the first gate runs `if: !cancelled()`, so a red one masks none of the others — the `om30` rule kept inside one job rather than by splitting it. (1) Lean, HARD: fail on any bare `import Mathlib` in content/**/*.lean; in this platform repo there is no content/, so the step prints SKIP and states that nothing was scanned. (2) Python, HARD: ruff F401 (unused) and F403 (wildcard) over the Python trees that exist, then the Python tests; an absent tree is dropped rather than passed to ruff, and an empty set says SKIP. (3) Dependency advisories, WARN-ONLY by the owner's ruling on bean `j41m`: is anything in the resolved tree KNOWN-VULNERABLE? The script exits 0 in every state and keeps them apart in its output; `.github/dependabot.yml` is the other half of that ruling and is not drawn here. (4) Rust wildcard imports, WARN-ONLY: report non-test `use …::*;` in tools/**/*.rs; `continue-on-error`, and therefore the job's LAST step, where it masks nothing."
msgstr ""

